-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ו/2 (20.1.2016): שכר עובדי הוראה בבעלויות על מוסדות החינוך ודיווחם
-- The owners' duty to report every teaching employee who teaches at their
-- institutions, whoever employs them, in every teaching hour; the ministry's
-- prohibition of "shoulder to shoulder" employment by another body; the duty
-- of another employing body to pay by law and the collective agreements;
-- and the owner's duty to pay its staff regardless of the ministry's funding.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ו/2 — שכר עובדי הוראה בבעלויות ודיווחם`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 The letterhead, the date (20.1.2016), the reference number, the addressee, the greeting and the subject line; no rule.
-- akn:hc_1/p14 The circular's purpose: to clarify the ministry's instructions on the duty to pay teaching staff at owners the ministry funds and supervises under the compulsory-education order, and the duty to report them; the duties follow.

-- This circular puts duties on a body that employs teachers at an owner's
-- school without being the owner; common.l4's parties do not name it, so the
-- circular has its own.
DECLARE `reporting party` IS ONE OF
    `the owner`
    `another employing body`

DECLARE `reporting action` IS ONE OF
    `report the teaching employee's hours to the ministry`
    `employ, in the regular curriculum, teachers the owner does not employ`
    `pay the teaching employee by law and the collective agreements` HAS `pay by the agreements` IS A NUMBER
    `pay the teaching employee all payments due` HAS `payments due paid` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `kind of teaching hour` IS ONE OF
    `frontal hour in class`
    `matriculation-preparation hour`
    `role hour`
    `individual hour`
    `teaching-support hour`
    `other teaching hour`

DECLARE `employer of the teacher` IS ONE OF
    `employed by the owner`
    `employed by a third-sector body`
    `employed by another body`

@desc One teaching hour a teaching employee gives at the owner's school.
DECLARE `teaching hour` HAS
    `hour kind`                 IS A `kind of teaching hour`
    `hour employer`             IS A `employer of the teacher`
    `budgeted by the ministry`  IS A BOOLEAN @desc within the ministry's standard for the school
    `funded from another source` IS A BOOLEAN

-- ¶15–¶16: the owner must report every teaching employee who teaches and is
-- employed at it, employed by the owner or by others (the third sector
-- included), beyond the ministry's standard. ¶17: in every teaching hour —
-- frontal, matriculation preparation, role, individual, teaching support
-- and others — those from other sources and those the ministry does not
-- budget included.
@ref akn:hc_1/p15 akn:hc_1/p16 akn:hc_1/p17
GIVEN h IS A `teaching hour`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the owner must report the hour` h IF
    TRUE

GIVEN `the reporting deadline` IS A NUMBER @desc the deadline for the report; the circular sets none (an input, in days)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reporting party` `reporting action`
DECIDE `reporting the hours` `the reporting deadline` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `report the teaching employee's hours to the ministry`
    WITHIN `the reporting deadline`
    LEST BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "circular 2015-16/2: the owner must report every teaching employee in every teaching hour at its school, whoever employs them"

-- ¶18: as a rule the ministry forbids employing, in the regular curriculum,
-- teaching staff not employed by the owner that holds the school's licence
-- ("shoulder to shoulder").
@ref akn:hc_1/p18
GIVEN `the school year's length` IS A NUMBER @desc in days
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reporting party` `reporting action`
DECIDE `no shoulder-to-shoulder employment` `the school year's length` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    SHANT `employ, in the regular curriculum, teachers the owner does not employ`
    WITHIN `the school year's length`
    LEST BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "circular 2015-16/2: as a rule, the ministry forbids teaching staff not employed by the licensed owner in the regular curriculum"

-- ¶19: where another body employs teaching staff at the institution doing
-- the same work as State or owner teachers in the regular hours, that body
-- must pay them by every law, the collective agreements for the stage and
-- type of school included.
@ref akn:hc_1/p19
GIVEN `same work in regular hours` IS A BOOLEAN @desc the work is the same as State or owner teachers' work, in the regular timetable
      `pay due by law and the agreements` IS A NUMBER @desc the pay the law and the collective agreements for the stage and type of school set; an input
      `the pay deadline` IS A NUMBER @desc when the pay falls due under the law and the agreements; the circular sets none (an input, in days)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reporting party` `reporting action`
DECIDE `the other body's duty to pay` `same work in regular hours` `pay due by law and the agreements` `the pay deadline` IS
    IF `same work in regular hours`
    THEN PARTY `another employing body`
         MUST  `pay the teaching employee by law and the collective agreements` `amount`
               PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `pay due by law and the agreements`
         WITHIN `the pay deadline`
         LEST BREACH BY `another employing body` BECAUSE "circular 2015-16/2: a body employing teachers in the same work in regular hours must pay them by law and the collective agreements"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- F-2015-16_tashav_02-a: ¶18 forbids "as a rule" (ככלל) and ¶19 opens
-- "however" (עם זאת) with the case of another body employing teachers in the
-- regular hours. Read as the exception "as a rule" leaves room for, ¶19
-- permits that employment where the body pays by the agreements; read as a
-- pay duty only, the employment stays forbidden. The reading adopted is the
-- second: ¶19 says who must pay and nowhere that the employment is allowed.
GIVEN `employed by another body` IS A BOOLEAN, `in the regular curriculum` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `forbidden by ¶18` `employed by another body` `in the regular curriculum` IF
    `employed by another body` AND `in the regular curriculum`

GIVEN `same work in regular hours` IS A BOOLEAN, `paid by law and the agreements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `allowed if ¶19 is the exception ¶18 leaves room for` `same work in regular hours` `paid by law and the agreements` IF
    `same work in regular hours` AND `paid by law and the agreements`

`¶18 and ¶19 give two answers for another body's teachers paid by the agreements` MEANS
        `forbidden by ¶18` TRUE TRUE
    AND `allowed if ¶19 is the exception ¶18 leaves room for` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `¶18 and ¶19 give two answers for another body's teachers paid by the agreements`

-- akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21 akn:hc_1/p22 A pointer to the Director-General's letter of 3.4.2014 and its web address (broken over two lines); no rule beyond those above.

-- ¶23: the owner must pay its teaching staff every payment they are due,
-- whether or not the ministry funds or indemnifies it.
@ref akn:hc_1/p23
GIVEN `payments due` IS A NUMBER
      `funded or indemnified by the ministry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the pay deadline` IS A NUMBER @desc when the payments fall due; the circular sets none (an input, in days)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `reporting party` `reporting action`
DECIDE `the owner's duty to pay` `payments due` `funded or indemnified by the ministry` `the pay deadline` IS
    PARTY `the owner`
    MUST  `pay the teaching employee all payments due` `amount`
          PROVIDED `amount` AT LEAST `payments due`
    WITHIN `the pay deadline`
    LEST BREACH BY `the owner` BECAUSE "circular 2015-16/2: the owner must pay its teaching staff every payment due, regardless of the ministry's funding or indemnity"

-- akn:conclusions The sign-off, the signature (Sonia Peretz) and the list of copies; no rule.

-- Worked examples. Time in days; the 30-day deadline given to the pay duties
-- is a placeholder input for a month's pay, which the circular does not name.
#ASSERT `the owner must report the hour` (`teaching hour` WITH `hour kind` IS `individual hour`, `hour employer` IS `employed by a third-sector body`, `budgeted by the ministry` IS FALSE, `funded from another source` IS TRUE)

#TRACE `the owner's duty to pay` 10000 FALSE 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `pay the teaching employee all payments due` 10000 AT 30
#TRACE `the other body's duty to pay` TRUE 8000 30 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `another employing body` DOES `pay the teaching employee by law and the collective agreements` 8000 AT 20
#TRACE `no shoulder-to-shoulder employment` 365 AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the owner` DOES `employ, in the regular curriculum, teachers the owner does not employ` AT 10
